What was KEPT from the upstream eval-viewer
-------------------------------------------
- Self-contained HTML: all review data is embedded into the page by replacing
  a single "/*__EMBEDDED_DATA__*/" marker, so the page works offline.
- Tiny stdlib-only HTTP server (http.server.BaseHTTPRequestHandler), no deps.
- Human verdicts auto-saved to feedback.json via a GET/POST /api/feedback
  endpoint; the "{reviews: [...]} object, validate then write" save contract.
- --previous-feedback diffing: prior feedback shown as context per record, and
  suppressing pre-fill from a stale on-disk feedback.json on a fresh iteration.
- --port flag, --static standalone-HTML export, keyboard navigation,
  "submit all" emits a row for EVERY record (so "no feedback" is
  distinguishable from "not reviewed").

What was CHANGED / ADDED
------------------------
- Replaced the skill-creator data model (a "run" = a directory containing an
  outputs/ subdir, with transcript.md / user_notes.md / grading.json
  conventions and a recursive find_runs() workspace scan) with lens-kit's flat
  JSON artifact model. A "record" is now one per-example / per-fixture /
  per-mutant row parsed from a results JSON file (parser.py).
- Added artifact-type detection (eval / calibration / mutation) by sniffing
  schema_version keys with a structural fallback.
- Added kind-specific rendering: per-lens verdict chips (tp/tn/fp/fn) with
  gold-vs-got + mismatch strings (eval); verdict vs acceptable/on-target
  (calibration); planted-defect marker + caught/missed (mutation); plus a
  per-artifact summary header (accuracy/catch/FP, acceptable/fp/fn rate,
  mutants-missed) and a variance-envelope block when present.
- feedback.json keys are "record_id" (the upstream used "run_id"); the loader
  reads either for backward compatibility.
- Records are fixed at server startup (no per-GET workspace re-scan), and the
  default port is 0 (OS-chosen ephemeral) — the upstream killed whoever held a
  fixed port via lsof; that behaviour was dropped.
- Stripped skill-creator-only notions (skill name, benchmark "with/without
  skill" tabs, file-embedding for images/pdf/xlsx outputs) that do not map to
  lens-kit artifacts.
